node_modules/
# the built extension of each release from 5.0.0 is committed (students install it from here); bundles,
# unpacked copies and test builds are not. dist/release/<version>/ holds each release with its signed
# checksums. The packages of 2.0.0 to 4.0.0 ask for an API key and were withdrawn on 2026-10-04
# (dist/release/README.md); only their records stay.
/dist/*
!/dist/beethoven-*.vsix
!/dist/release/
extension/dist/
dist-test/
out/
.vscode-test/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# never commit credentials
*.token
*.env
!*.env.example
secrets*
.credentials.json
# build intermediates for the manual
docs/build/

# license signing keys never enter the repository (they live in the vendor folder ~/.beethoven-vendor,
# ~/.ashley-vendor before the rename); the one exception is the test-only key that test builds trust
*.pem
!extension/test-fixtures/license/test-signing-key.pem
.beethoven-vendor/
.ashley-vendor/
extension/build-meta/
.wrangler/
